# Copy to .env.local and fill in. None of these are required for the app to run.

# PostHog analytics (see src/utils/posthog.ts). Both values are public — the
# token is a write-only ingestion key, and the host is a managed reverse proxy
# on our own domain (so ad blockers that list *.posthog.com don't drop events)
# rather than PostHog's direct ingestion endpoint. Unset → PostHog stays
# disabled and every helper in posthog.ts is a no-op.
# In Vercel both are scoped to Production — previews and dev never report in.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN=
# Direct ingestion (no proxy) would be https://eu.i.posthog.com — note the `.i.`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://f.qingqi.dev
